    This is important: <strong>Picmal never uploads your images anywhere</strong
    >. Everything happens on your Mac. I don't see your images, I don't track
    what you convert, and I don't collect any personal data from the app.
  </p>

  <p>
    The website (picmal.app) uses PostHog (EU-hosted) for privacy-friendly
    analytics—visitor counts, which pages convert, and anonymous session
    recordings to spot usability issues. That's separate from the app and
    doesn't involve your images.
  </p>

  <p>
    Check out the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> if you want more details.
  </p>

